{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917308986},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find the total number of farmers markets in the U.S. from a dataset\n2. Get census data (residents/population)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Express to four decimal places\n5. Use tools to do the math (not hand calculation)\n6. Only state verified facts from the catalog\n\nAccording to the AGENTS.md instructions, I should:\n1. First check `xorq_semantic_models` to see if there's a relevant semantic model\n2. Then `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see what's available\n3. Only ingest sources if needed\n4. Never hand-calculate - use xorq_select to compute values\n5. Verify with xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking what's already in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012heF2qHNqGozYYDsBci8VT","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012FWgvJ6oDFAErXEPUrU6SZ","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":340,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8306,"totalTokens":8656,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.